"Stephen Lattanzi" <lattanzi@myeastern.com> wrote:

>Thanks.  I used cacls to change permissions to allow full access to all 
>users on all files in the NetHack directory, but it still didn't work.  I 
>then moved the installation from C:\Program Files\NetHack to C:\NetHack, and 
>this solved the problem--at least for the tty version.
>
>When I try to run the graphical interface version on a non-Administrator 
>account, it seems to work, but I get the error message "Cannot write record 
>record" when the game starts, and the error message "Cannot write logfile!" 
>at the end of the game.  Any suggestions?

Both interface versions should not behave differently in any way. I would
check the following things: Does the tty vesion really write to the
logfile, or does it just not show the error message? What happens when
you log in as a user and directly create files in the NetHack directory,
and what if you modify existing files? Did NetHack try to write to
"c:\program\logfile", being confused by the space in the directory name?
Can filemon (http://www.sysinternals.com/Utilities/Filemon.html) help? 

